e Sunday afternoon, increasing\nthe threat for flash flooding across vulnerable terrain. While\nconfidence in location and rainfall rates remain low at this time,\nthe potential for rapidly rising rivers, streams, normally dry\narroyos and slot canyons are possible Sunday through Monday.\n\nPlease follow the evolving forecast, especially if your plans\nincluding recreating or commuting across eastern Utah and western\nColorado Sunday onward. Also, keep in mind weather potential above\nyour location and upstream, particularly for those who reside below\nsensitive terrain like recent burn scars.","ends":"2026-10-12T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; Delta, CO; Dolores, CO; Garfield, CO; Hinsdale, CO; La Plata, CO; Mesa, CO; Moffat, CO; Montezuma, CO; Montrose, CO; Ouray, CO; Rio Blanco, CO; San Juan, CO; San Miguel, CO; Daggett, UT; Grand, UT; San Juan, UT; Uintah, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5953c0ab1d0bcab0b29fc3e9364e3d17cf28daf6.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5953c0ab1d0bcab0b29fc3e9364e3d17cf28daf6.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-10T17:52:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 101752 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1152 AM MDT Sat Oct 10 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Moisture increases this weekend as remnants of tropical system Rachel move through the region, especially this evening through Sunday. Rainfall totals of 1-2 inches and locally higher are possible over the eastern Utah mountains and the San Juans. Moderat","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-10T08:45:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... Remnant moisture from Tropical Storm Rachel will filter into the region today. Wetting rains are expected to develop across the region by early this evening, with some isolated showers and thunderstorms expected by this morning. Strong winds